# --- uses: ["core"] builtins are doc-local at the type-checker level.
# Runtime isolation is deferred (S-786 Phase 4). At runtime, core builtins are
# accessible in all documents because core builtins are in stdlib_env globally.
# The type checker enforces isolation via T002: both the second and third documents
# lack a --- uses: header, so the type checker warns about raw builtins in each.
# Two T002 warnings are expected: one for builtin-if (doc 2) and one for builtin-add (doc 3).
--- uses: ["core"]
---
[x: [builtin-if true 1 0]]
---
[y: [builtin-add 3 4]]
=== out
Dict({"y": Int(7)})
=== warn
raw builtin `builtin-if` is not available in user code
raw builtin `builtin-add` is not available in user code
